e focus on the confirmed subtitle-missing-after-rotation bug and report it. But before reporting, let me make sure the quote and element ref are right. The element showing the missing subtitle is [1] \"Spanish\" (toolbar_content). The expected is \"Spanish / 4 cards shown\". Since the bug is about missing text, I can leave observed_quote out? The instructions say: \"a report about something missing may leave the quote out, but a quote that was never on screen gets the report rejected.\" I can quote the on-screen text that shows the defect: the header shows only \"Spanish\" whereas it should also show \"4 cards shown\". Hmm, quoting \"Spanish\" is valid on-screen text. But the defect is missing subtitle. I'll use observed_quote \"Spanish\" maybe. Actually better: observed could be \"Header shows only 'Spanish' with no card count subtitle\". The element_ref should be 1 (toolbar_content). Let me file.\n\nBut wait — is the subtitle really missing, or is it just not rendered in the accessibility tree? The screenshot confirms visually there's only \"Spanish\". Yes.\n\nLet me also double-check the initial state had subtitle: yes, element [1] \"LinearLayout contains 'Spanish' | '4 cards shown'\". Confirmed.\n\nLet me file this bug now.\n\nScreen: Card browser\nElement: Toolbar / header subtitle\nField: subtitle (\"N cards shown\")\nSymptom type: missing\nExpected: After rotating the device (or recreating the screen), the card browser header should still show \"Spanish\" with subtitle \"4 cards shown\".\nObserved: After rotation, the header shows only \"Spanish\"; the \"4 cards shown\" subtitle is missing.\nSteps: Open Card browser -> header shows \"Spanish / 4 cards shown\" -> rotate to landscape and back to portrait -> subtitle disappears.\n\nelement_ref: 1. observed_quote: \"Spanish\". Hmm, the \"observed quote\" should show the defect. Quoting \"Spanish\" is what's shown. I'll include that. Actually, the instructions say \"exact text you saw on screen that shows the defect (copy it verbatim from an observation, e.g. the wrong value or the label shown)\". For a missing element, the closest element's text \"Spanish\" is acceptable. I'll quote \"Spanish\".\n\nLet me file the report."}
