{"type": "thinking", "text": "With \"All decks\" filter and query \"tag:verb\", the browser finds comer (1 card shown). This confirms the \"Search all decks\" snackbar action is broken: from the French deck, tapping \"Search all decks\" should do the same but instead shows an empty list.\n\nLet me now verify the exact behavior right after \"Search all decks\" with a fresh reproduction, to ensure I describe it accurately. I already did it twice: both times empty list. Let me capture the observed state for the report. I'll reproduce once more quickly:\n- Collapse search (returns to All decks 7 cards).\n- Switch to French.\n- Search tag:verb.\n- Tap Search all decks.\n- Observe empty list.\n\nActually, I have enough evidence: two reproductions. The bug: \"Search all decks\" action on the snackbar doesn't run the search across all decks; it leaves the deck filter unchanged (still French) and shows an empty result list.\n\nHmm, wait. Could it be that tapping \"Search all decks\" actually changes the deck scope to All decks but the *query* gets reset to empty? No: after tapping, the search field still showed \"tag:verb\" and the list was empty. If the query were reset to empty and scope All decks, it would show 7 cards (not empty). If scope French and query empty, 3 cards. Empty means both query tag:verb and scope French (no matches). So the action did nothing except clear the list/snackbar and re-run the same French-scoped search? Hmm, actually, the list was empty before the action too (0 results). So the action effectively didn't change anything except dismiss the snackbar. So \"Search all decks\" does nothing.\n\nThis is a legitimate bug in browsing/searching. Let me file it.\n\nHowever — is \"Search all decks\" actually supposed to work in this version? It's a visible button, so yes. And it's in the browsing/searching area. Let me file.\n\nScreen: Card browser\nElement: snackbar \"Search all decks\" button\nField: cross-deck search action\nSymptom: no_effect\nExpected: Tapping \"Search all decks\" runs the search across all decks and shows the matching card (comer, 1 card).\nObserved: After tapping \"Search all decks\", the results list is empty; the deck filter remains French, so the matching card in Spanish is never shown.\nSteps: select French deck filter; open Search; type tag:verb; submit -> \"No cards found in deck 'French'\" snackbar; tap \"Search all decks\" -> empty list, filter still French.\nelement_ref: 9 (the snackbar action, from the latest observe where it existed; but note the latest observe now is different). The element_ref refers to \"your latest observation\". Currently my latest observe after pressing Search shows element 8 comer, 9 snackbar \"1 card shown\". Hmm. The search all decks button is no longer present. I should perhaps re-reproduce and file with the element ref from that observation. But the tool says element_ref from latest observe. It's okay to use the appropriate element; the developer will check. Let me reproduce once more to have the snackbar action visible and file with its ref. But I can also file now with element_ref from the previous observation? The instructions: \"element_ref: number of the element showing the defect, from your latest observe\". So I should do an observe where the \"Search all decks\" button is visible, then file.\n\nLet me reproduce once more (quick) and file immediately after the observe showing the snackbar action (before tapping it, the defect is about the button's effect — hmm, the defect is observed after tapping, when the snackbar is gone). The element showing the defect after tapping is the empty list area. There's no element with text. Hmm, this is a \"missing\" symptom: the matching card is missing from the results. The closest element is the toolbar/deck filter or the empty list. The \"No cards found\" snackbar is gone.\n\nI could file with element_ref of the deck filter toolbar_content (showing \"French\") — but in search mode the toolbar_content isn't present. Hmm.\n\nMaybe I should file while the snackbar \"No cards found in deck 'French'\" with \"Search all decks\" is showing, describing that pressing it has no effect. The element_ref could be 9 (the Search all decks button). The observed_quote could be \"No cards found in deck 'French'\" (on screen) — but that's the pre-tap state. The defect is the no_effect of the button. The quote can be the button's label \"Search all decks\" (element 9). That is on screen at that moment. Good.\n\nLet me reproduce once more to get a fresh observation with the snackbar action visible, then file.\n\nSteps: Currently All decks with tag:verb showing comer. Collapse, switch to French, search tag:verb, observe snackbar, then file using that observation. Then optionally tap Search all decks again to confirm.\n\nActually, I've confirmed twice already. Let me just reproduce to the snackbar state and file. Then I'll also tap to reconfirm? I've done it twice. I'll file immediately.\n\nLet me collapse and switch to French."}
