 triggered by long-press, and it shows the current card's values for each column so you can decide which to display. It would have checkboxes on the left in the real UI, but the accessibility tree might not expose them, and the screenshot might not show them if they're custom. Looking at the screenshot again: each row is a label + value, with no checkbox visible. It looks like a card info dialog, not a column manager. Hmm.\n\nHmm, actually, maybe it IS the \"Card info\" dialog with the *wrong title*. But the dialog's content includes \"Question\", \"Answer\", \"Tags\"... which is the card info. The title should be \"Card info\" or \"Info\". \"Manage column\" is wrong. Would AnkiDroid have a \"Manage column\" dialog with card info content? Unlikely.\n\nBut wait — perhaps the dialog is the **\"Manage column\" from the card browser's column header long-press**, and its purpose is to let you choose the *sort column* by showing each column's name and a sample value. The \"Question\"/\"Answer\"/\"Tags\"/... labels are column names, and the values are sample values. It might not have checkboxes because tapping a row selects that column for display? Hmm. But \"Question\"/\"Answer\" aren't actual columns in the browser (the columns are Sort Field, Card Type, Due, Deck, Tags, Ease, ...). The dialog includes \"Question\" and \"Answer\", which are card info fields, not browser columns. So it's card info.\n\nHmm, but maybe the \"Manage column\" dialog lists ALL possible columns including Question/Answer; the browser could show Question/Answer columns? The visible table only shows Sort Field, Card Type, Due, Deck. But the sort dialog lists Sort Field, Card Type, Due, Deck, Tags, Ease, Card Modified, Created, Note Modified, Interval — no Question/Answer. Hmm.\n\nActually, the \"Manage column\" dialog content matches the \"Card info\" fields exactly: Question, Answer, Tags, Ease, Card Modified, Created, Note Modified, Interval, Lapses, Note Type, Reviews. So it's the card info dialog. The title \"Manage column\" is wrong. Hmm, unless the card info dialog is titled \"Manage column\" by mistake in this build. That's a plausible bug: tapping the Due column header (or the first card?) shows the card info dialog with the wrong title.\n\nHold on — maybe I actually tapped the card row, not the header. The element tap for element 7 was at (675,294). The card row starts at y≈350. The center (675,294) is 56px above the first row. So it's the header. But the dialog content is the card info for bonjour. So tapping the \"Due\" header opens card info for the first card. That could be the intended behavior of tapping a column header? No, tapping a header should sort by that column or open a menu.\n\nWait, maybe in AnkiDroid, tapping a column header opens a menu with options:\n- \"Sort ascending\"\n- \"Sort descending\"\n- \"Manage column\"?\nand the accessibility tree's \"Manage column\" title plus card info rows... Hmm, no.\n\nLet me test tapping other headers (Sort Field, Card Type, Deck) to see if they also open the same \"Manage column\" dialog. If they all do, maybe it's the column header's context dialog (and the card info content is intended to preview). If only \"Due\" does, maybe it's a mis-wired bug.\n\nActually, the sort dialog is opened via overflow > Change display order. So tapping a column header may open a *different* dialog: \"Manage column\" which shows the column's info. Hmm.\n\nLet me test tapping the \"Sort Field\" header (element 5) and see what dialog appears. Then \"Deck\" (8). If they show \"Manage column\" with different contents (e.g., a list of options), it's intended. Let me test.\n\nI'm currently in Appearance. Let me go back to the card browser via drawer > Card browser. Press back to Settings, then back? The browser was in the back stack? Actually we came from the browser? No, we came from the deck list via drawer > Settings > ... Let me open the drawer from Settings? Settings doesn't have a drawer. Press back twice to deck list, then drawer > Card browser.\n\nHmm, wait: Current navigation: deck list -> drawer -> Settings -> Appearance. Pressing back -> Settings, back -> deck list. Then drawer -> Card browser. Let me do that.\n\nActually, before going down this path, let me evaluate whether this \"Manage column\" thing is in scope and likely a real bug. The task says sweep \"browsing and searching cards\". A dialog m", "truncated": true}
